<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Offset</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path">tree context menu for</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Datum Plane &gt; Offset</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Offset</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command translates a datum plane along its normal.</span></p>
<p><img src="../view_menu/Using_Datums_files/image108.gif" width="288px" height="192px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Offset plane</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Offset amount. If the value is positive the offset is on the normal direction. Otherwise it is opposite to the normal direction. Default value is 3mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Create copy</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Check this option to generate new plane with the modified location. If unchecked the plane to which the command is applied, is translated.</span></p>
